description: Found reviewing #53 at fd64121. The labels pass in checks/corpus-lint.sh prints one line per issue and topic, and the row pass adds the allowance for every matching line, so one live issue labelled both of a row's topics counts twice against that row.
 
 Reproduced: three files staged into corpus/emit (base 10, topics lang/fns,host) with one live issue labelled corpus:lang/fns and corpus:host pass at 13 files, where the rule gives 12. The wasm row (lang,host) has the same shape for any issue tagged a lang/* topic plus host.
 
 Fix: carry the issue id on each labels line and skip an id the row has already counted. One awk change; checks/corpus-lint.sh with CORPUS_LINT_NOTES pointed at scratch refs is the test shape.
